  "finding": "Explicit contiguous head-first inputs still leave the cosine multiply token-first in native IR, with native output bitwise equal to token-first. Flattening head/token rows changes the native cosine multiply to [1,12,T,128] with [1,1,T,128] phases. On seeded BF16 inputs, flat output matches CPU bitwise at both512 and4096 tokens; baseline relative L2 is about0.00055/0.00065. At4096, measured kernel+output-transfer median falls28.06ms to12.60ms (2.23x); at512 it increases4.17ms to4.44ms. These are kernel results, not full-flow measurements.",
